{
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "title": "Getting started",
   "kind": "intro",
   "items": [],
   "pages": [
    {
     "title": "Set up your camera",
     "body": "Sit with light in front of you, not behind. Keep both shoulders and your hands in view. A plain wall behind you helps."
    },
    {
     "title": "Your dominant hand leads",
     "body": "Sign with the hand you write with. Left-handed signers are supported: SignBridge mirrors what it sees."
    },
    {
     "title": "Rest between signs",
     "body": "Lower your hands after each sign. That is how SignBridge knows a sign has ended and the next one can start."
    },
    {
     "title": "Your face is grammar",
     "body": "Raised eyebrows ask a yes or no question. Lowered eyebrows ask what, where or who. SignBridge reads both."
    },
    {
     "title": "Spell what has no sign",
     "body": "Fingerspelling covers names and any word without its own sign. Letters and numbers have their own lessons."
    }
   ]
  },
